# Cursor Rules — W0lfSword iOS Exploit Knowledge Base

## Workspace Configuration
This workspace contains a curated iOS exploit development knowledge base.
Skills are in `skills/` and research docs in `docs/`.

## Context Injection Rules

### Auto-load these files when relevant keywords appear:

**Kernel Exploitation** (PAC, SMR, IOSurface, KASLR, socket spray, offsets, Checkm8, PPL):
→ Always include `@skills/ios-kernel-exploit.md`

**Sandbox Escape** (SSV, TCC, vnode, containermanagerd, MAC framework, MIG bypass, path traversal):
→ Always include `@skills/ios-sandbox-escape.md`

**Security Testing** (Frida, AMFI, CoreTrust, code signing, bug bounty, YARA, SSL pinning):
→ Always include `@skills/ios-security-pentesting.md`

**Tooling & Build** (Theos, ldid, libimobiledevice, kernelcache, deploy, dpkg-deb):
→ Always include `@skills/ios-misc-tooling.md`

**Research & Findings** (bounty reports, exploit architecture, deep dive):
→ Always include `@docs/researchdeepseek.md`

## Offsets Rule
Never hallucinate iOS kernel struct offsets. Always reference the skill files or suggest offset discovery methods (KDK, XPF, runtime validation).

## Citation Format
When answering, cite the skill file and section: `skills/ios-kernel-exploit.md §3.1`

## Project Structure
- `skills/` — 4 AI agent skill files with YAML frontmatter
- `projects/` — 10 reference exploit repositories
- `docs/` — Research documents and findings
- `.claude/` — Claude Code configuration
- `.codex.md` — OpenAI Codex configuration
- `opencode.json` — OpenCode configuration
